%N A400913 For n >= 1, a(n) is the smallest twin prime representable as the sum of 2*n - 1 consecutive terms of A001097, the sequence of twin primes.
%e A400913 2081 is the smallest twin prime that can be expressed as the sum of 2*8 - 1 = 15 consecutive twin primes, namely, 71, 73, 101, 103, 107, 109, 137, 139, 149, 151, 179, 181, 191, 193, and 197. So a(8) = 2081.
